OL,3,GNEWSAHow a giant cockerel sculpture
OL,4,Abecame a celebrity
OL,5,
OL,6,FA giant silver cockerel that stands on
OL,7,Fa roundabout overlooking passing
OL,8,Ftraffic in Dorking has become one of
OL,9,FSurrey's most recognisable landmarks.
OL,11,FThe unusual piece of public art
OL,12,Fcelebrates a bird with deep roots in
OL,13,Fthe town's history, a museum curator
OL,14,Fhas told Secret Surrey.
OL,16,FKathy Atherton, from Dorking Museum,
OL,17,Fsaid the Dorking chicken has been
OL,18,Fassociated with the town for centuries.
OL,19,F"The Dorkings have been bred here at
OL,20,Fleast since the 17th Century," she
OL,21,Fsaid.
OL,23,APub: 13-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
